        <definition>SFML_AUDIO_API std::optional&lt; std::string &gt; sf::PlaybackDevice::getDefaultDevice</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>getDefaultDevice</name>
        <qualifiedname>sf::PlaybackDevice::getDefaultDevice</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Get the name of the default audio playback device. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function returns the name of the default audio playback device. If none is available, <computeroutput>std::nullopt</computeroutput> is returned.</para>
<para>Note that depending on when this function is called, the default device reported by the operating system might change e.g. when a USB audio device is plugged into or unplugged from the system.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>The name of the default audio playback device </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
